<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cincinnatus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as Lucius Quinctius Cincinnatus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucius Quinctius Cincinnatus was a Roman statesman of the 5th century BCE. According to tradition he was called from ploughing his farm in 458 BCE to serve as dictator, rescued a Roman army trapped by the Aequi on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-algidus">Mount Algidus</a>, and gave up his power after sixteen days to return to the plough. He became the Roman model of civic virtue.</p></div>
